// MD-102 Episode 7: device query (single device, KQL)
//
// What it does: ask one Windows device for its live state.
//   Intune admin center › Devices › Windows › select the device › Monitor › Device query › paste ONE query › Run.
// Requirements: Advanced Analytics (Intune Suite add-on, episode 11); corporate-owned Windows device that is
//   Entra joined or hybrid joined; Windows Push Notification Services (WNS) must not be blocked.
// Role (least privilege): a custom Intune role with Managed Devices/Query, plus read access to managed devices
//   (for example Organization/Read, Managed devices/Read).
// Supported table operators: count, distinct, join, order by, project, take, top, where.
// Validated against Microsoft Learn ("Device query", "Intune Data Platform schema"); not run against a tenant.

// The episode's query: is the drive encrypted? (columns from the EncryptableVolume table)
EncryptableVolume
| project WindowsDriveLetter, ProtectionStatus, EncryptionPercentage

// Is the print spooler running? (WindowsService table)
WindowsService
| where ServiceName == "Spooler"
| project ServiceName, DisplayName, State

// BIOS details (BiosInfo table)
BiosInfo
| project Manufacturer, SerialNumber, ReleaseDateTime
